  "tagline": "Open-source MUMPS/M hierarchical key-value database forked from GT.M, with SQL via Octo.",
  "description": "YottaDB is a high-performance hierarchical key-value database descended from GT.M, which it forked in 2017 to develop in the open. Data lives in persistent sparse arrays (M globals) with ACID transactions, journaling and logical multi-site replication, and it serves core-banking and VistA electronic health record systems around the world. Beyond the M language it offers native APIs for C, Go, Rust, Python, Node.js, Perl and Lua, and Octo adds SQL over the PostgreSQL wire protocol. It is the go-to engine for keeping M applications alive on modern Linux.",
